  "_rebuild_todo": {
    "note": "Tracking list for continuing this rebuild in future sessions -- not consumed by the app, reference only.",
    "remaining_ferial_evening": "Ferial Ramsha is now complete for 12 of 14 day/cycle combinations (all of Monday-Thursday in both Qdham and Wathar, plus Friday-Qdham and Saturday-Wathar). Two gaps remain: Saturday-Qdham (no source text obtained yet -- only 'First Saturday', which is the Wathar form, has been located) and Friday-Wathar ('Last Friday' -- text obtained through the Evening Anthem but cuts off before the prayer/Shuraya-instead-of-Letter-Psalm/Martyrs' Anthem; deliberately not built rather than publish an incomplete Martyrs' Anthem, same reasoning as the original Friday gap). Sunday's evening service is NOT ferial -- it lives in the separate Festival Evening Service section (Maclean p.68 onward) and has not been started.",
    "festival_evening": "Maclean p.68 onward -- distinct from ferial, used Sundays/feasts/memorials.",
    "night_service_lelya": "Maclean p.85 onward (ferial), p.151 onward (festival).",
    "morning_service_sapra": "Maclean p.103 onward (ferial), p.165 onward (festival).",
    "compline_subaa": "Maclean p.185 onward -- Maclean notes Compline is 'now almost obsolete, except on certain days of the year, when it is usually joined on to the Evening Service' (Introduction, p.xii-xiii). Worth confirming with Josh whether to build this as a standalone office or documented as a rare joined-on addition, matching what the source actually says about its use.",
    "minor_hours": "Maclean documents these only as 'relics of Terce and Sext in the Fast' (p.219, 224, 'Prayer at noon') -- NOT a routine daily set of texts. The current app's cathedral/monastic Third/Sixth/Ninth Hour sequences (all deleted this session) had no basis in Maclean at all. Needs a decision from Josh: keep minor hours out of scope entirely (matching how Maclean scopes them), or find a separate source for full monastic minor-hour texts if that's wanted (Maclean's own stated scope excludes the full Khudhra/Geza/Kashkul, which is where any fuller monastic-hour material would live).",
    "cathedral_vs_monastic": "Maclean's book does not describe two parallel 'Cathedral' and 'Monastic' forms of each hour the way the deleted build assumed -- it describes ONE ferial form and, separately, festival/Sunday/memorial forms. Where the historical Cathedral/monastic distinction actually shows up in Church of the East practice (if at all, in the sources available) needs to be researched properly before rebuilding this axis, not assumed.",
    "of_our_father_prayer": "Maclean's original names the reigning Catholicos and a patron saint explicitly (Mar Awa at the time of writing, 1894). Currently rendered generically pending a decision on how -- or whether -- to handle a living officeholder's name, which the app has no existing mechanism for keeping current.",
    "seasonal_material": "Anything proper to the Khudhra/Geza/Kashkul (the three large cyclical books covering seasons and specific holy days) is explicitly OUTSIDE Maclean's stated scope (Introduction, p.xi) and will need a separate source if wanted -- flagged as a gap, not guessed at."
  },
